       <h1>BJP Questions Congress After Court Order on Sonia Gandhi’s Electoral Roll Entry</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#BJP</span> <span>#Congress</span> <span>#Sonia Gandhi</span> <span>#Electoral Roll</span></div>
       <p>The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) has raised questions concerning the Congress party following a recent court order pertaining to Sonia Gandhi's entry into the electoral roll. A Delhi court has directed a Magistrate to investigate a complaint alleging that Ms. Gandhi was added to the voters’ list prior to her acquiring Indian citizenship.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-22/bjp-questions-congress-after-court-order-on-sonia-gandhis-el.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This development has brought renewed attention to the circumstances surrounding Ms. Gandhi's enrollment as a voter. The complaint at the heart of the court's directive suggests a potential procedural irregularity regarding the timing of her registration in relation to her citizenship status. The court's instruction for a Magisterial inquiry indicates a judicial acknowledgment of the need to examine the allegations thoroughly.</p><p>The BJP's questioning of the Congress underscores the political ramifications of the court's decision. The opposition party appears to be leveraging the judicial development to scrutinize the Congress leadership and its historical records. This issue could potentially become a point of contention in the ongoing political discourse.</p><p>The directive mandates the Magistrate to look into the specifics of the complaint, which centers on the timeline of Ms. Gandhi's citizenship acquisition versus her inclusion in the electoral rolls. The outcome of this inquiry will be crucial in clarifying the facts surrounding the allegations. Both parties are likely to closely monitor the proceedings as the investigation unfolds.</p><p>What to watch: The findings of the Magisterial inquiry and subsequent political reactions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article strictly adheres to the details in the source summary regarding the court directive and Sonia Gandhi's electoral roll complaint.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/bjp-questions-congress-after-court-order-on-sonias-electoral-roll-entry/article71495923.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
