     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-22 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cyber Police Warn Against Fake Share Investment Frauds</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cybersecurity</span> <span>#Fraud</span> <span>#Police Advisory</span> <span>#Financial Crime</span></div>
       <p>The Cyber Police have issued a significant advisory, specifically warning the public against the proliferation of fake share investment frauds. This proactive measure by law enforcement agencies underscores an apparent rise in sophisticated financial scams targeting individuals through deceptive investment schemes.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-22/cyber-police-warn-against-fake-share-investment-frauds.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The advisory's primary objective is to safeguard potential victims from falling prey to fraudulent opportunities masquerading as legitimate stock or share market ventures. While the specifics of the warning's content have not been detailed, its overarching message is clear: to alert citizens to the inherent risks associated with unsolicited or suspicious investment propositions.</p><p>The move by the Cyber Police highlights the persistent threat posed by online financial deception. It serves as a crucial reminder for the public to maintain vigilance and exercise extreme caution when approached with investment offers, particularly those that promise unrealistic returns with minimal risk. Such advisories are critical in fostering greater public awareness and promoting safer online financial practices, thereby mitigating the impact of these prevalent frauds.</p><p>What to watch: Increased public vigilance against online financial scams and continued efforts by cyber authorities to combat digital fraud.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/cyber-police-issue-advisory-against-fake-share-investment-frauds/article71496104.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
