     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Demolition Looms for Shastri and Krishi Bhawans in Delhi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Government</span> <span>#Delhi</span> <span>#Infrastructure</span> <span>#Urban Development</span></div>
       <p>The iconic Shastri Bhawan and Krishi Bhawan in Delhi are set for demolition, marking a significant change in the capital's administrative landscape. Occupants of these Central government complexes have been directed to vacate the premises by September 30.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-22/demolition-looms-for-shastri-and-krishi-bhawans-in-delhi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This directive paves the way for the construction of new government offices, specifically Kartavya Bhawan 4 and 5. Both buildings currently house several crucial Central government complexes, making their impending demolition a notable development for various ministries and departments. The September 30 deadline underscores the urgency of the transition, as preparations for the new construction projects appear to be moving forward swiftly.</p><p>The move is part of a broader initiative to redevelop government infrastructure within the capital. The introduction of Kartavya Bhawan 4 and 5 suggests an expansion or modernization of office spaces designed to accommodate Central government operations. This transition will necessitate the relocation of numerous government personnel and departments, leading to a substantial logistical undertaking in the coming months. The demolition of these long-standing structures signifies a tangible step towards new architectural and functional paradigms for government workspaces in Delhi.</p><p>What to watch: The relocation of government offices and the commencement of new construction.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Article faithfully reflects source; adds minor detail about demolition not in source but not contradictory.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/stage-set-for-demolition-of-shastri-bhawan-and-krishi-bhawan-in-delhi/article71495723.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="article/2026-09-22/demolition-looms-for-shastri-and-krishi-bhawans-in-delhi.html" data-title="Demolition Looms for Shastri and Krishi Bhawans in Delhi"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
