     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-09-22 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Netflix Launches 'Kpop Demon Hunters' Ticketed Experience</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Netflix</span> <span>#Kpop Demon Hunters</span> <span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Immersive Experience</span></div>
       <p>Netflix is expanding its physical entertainment offerings by bringing the world of “Kpop Demon Hunters” to life outside the screen. The streamer has unveiled “Kpop Demon Hunters: The Immersive Experience,” a ticketed attraction designed to engage fans of its blockbuster animated film. This initiative marks a significant step in Netflix’s strategy to diversify its content delivery beyond digital platforms.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-22/netflix-launches-kpop-demon-hunters-ticketed-experience.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The immersive experience will debut at Netflix House locations, starting in Dallas and Philadelphia. The attraction is scheduled to open on November 12 at Netflix House Dallas, followed by its launch at the Philadelphia location on November 20. By leveraging its existing physical spaces, Netflix aims to create a multi-sensory environment that mirrors the aesthetic and narrative elements of the film. This approach allows the company to monetize its intellectual property through direct consumer engagement rather than relying solely on subscription revenue.</p><p>The move underscores the growing trend of streaming services investing in experiential entertainment. As competition intensifies, Netflix is seeking new ways to deepen audience connection with its original content. The “Kpop Demon Hunters” experience is expected to draw significant attention given the film’s popularity. Details regarding ticket pricing and specific interactive features were not disclosed in the initial announcement.</p><p>What to watch: The initial audience reception and attendance figures for the Dallas and Philadelphia openings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary regarding dates and locations. The analysis regarding Netflix's strategy is speculative but acceptable as editorial commentary, not contradictory fact.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/shopping/news/kpop-demon-hunters-immersive-experience-netflix-tickets-1236872059/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
