       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-09-22 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Trump Predicts Swift End to Ukraine War</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ukraine War</span> <span>#US Diplomacy</span> <span>#UN General Assembly</span> <span>#International Relations</span></div>
       <p>President Donald Trump has stated that the war in Ukraine will end &quot;more quickly than people understand.&quot; The President made these remarks while addressing the United Nations General Assembly in New York. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-22/trump-predicts-swift-end-to-ukraine-war.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During his address, Trump emphasized that his administration is &quot;working very closely with the leaders of Russia and Ukraine.&quot; He expressed confidence in the diplomatic efforts currently underway, suggesting that a resolution is imminent. </p><p>The President’s comments signal a shift in tone regarding the timeline for ending the conflict. By asserting that the process will be faster than anticipated, he aims to project a sense of urgency and progress in US diplomatic engagements. </p><p>The statement underscores the active role the US is taking in mediating between the two belligerent parties. The phrase &quot;working very closely&quot; indicates high-level communications and coordination with both Moscow and Kyiv. </p><p>This approach contrasts with previous periods of uncertainty regarding the duration of the war. The President’s confidence in a swift resolution may influence international expectations and market reactions to the ongoing conflict. </p><p>The remarks were delivered to a global audience, reinforcing the US commitment to seeking a peaceful and expeditious conclusion to the hostilities. The focus remains on direct engagement with the key stakeholders involved in the war. </p><p>What to watch: Specific diplomatic milestones or announcements from Russian and Ukrainian leaders following the UN session.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/will-get-that-done-trump-says-ukraine-war-will-end-more-quickly-than-people-understand-10346755.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
